            <h1 id="schrift-shop-title" class="type-display-2xl case-hero__title">
              <span>Schrift Shop.</span>
              <span class="case-hero__title-muted">A typography-first commerce layer for books, specimens, and collective editions</span>
            </h1>
          </div>

          <div class="case-hero__grid">
            <div class="type-heading-lg case-hero__summary">
              <p>Schrift Shop is the retail arm of Schrift Collective — a place where publishing, type specimens, and small-batch editions share one calm system. The work focused on clarity at checkout without dulling the editorial presence that defines the collective.</p>
              <p>The challenge was to carry an exhibition-like catalogue attitude into carts, fulfilment states, and account surfaces — keeping rhythm, hierarchy, and specimen detail readable while the infrastructure stays pragmatic.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="case-content-shell" aria-label="Case content">
        <div class="case-content">
          <section class="case-text-block" aria-label="Schrift Shop context">
            <p class="type-caption case-note">
              Context · See also <a class="case-note__link" href="{{ "/schrift-foundry/" | url }}">Schrift Foundry case</a>
            </p>

            <div class="type-body-lg case-prose">
              <p>The shop sits beside the foundry catalogue and journal — three fronts of one practice. Where the foundry foregrounds licensing and deep type narratives, the shop handles objects readers can hold: printed matter, specimens, editions, and occasional collaborations.</p>
              <p>Early conversations centred on reuse: extending the collective’s existing graphic language rather than inventing a parallel brand. Product templates, typography scales, and imagery treatments had to align with editorial pages already in production.</p>
              <p>This page documents the layout system as shipped — narrative blocks alternate with commerce visuals so stakeholders can see both storytelling rhythm and shelf mechanics in one scroll.</p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="case-text-block" aria-label="Schrift Shop positioning">
            <div class="type-body-lg case-prose">
              <p>We treated categories as curated lanes rather than catalogue dumps — each lane keeps one typographic voice dominant while filters stay lightweight. Photography follows specimen discipline: cropped honestly, labelled sizes, and surfaces that respect paper grain instead of flattening everything into hero composites.</p>
              <p>Microcopy mirrors the collective tone — concise, slightly archival, never shouty — while transactional modules borrow spacing from editorial margins so checkout feels like continuation, not a separate product.</p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="schrift-shop-media-grid" aria-label="Schrift Shop storefront explorations">
            <figure class="schrift-shop-media schrift-shop-media--01" data-reveal="scale">
              <img src="{{ "/assets/figma/schrift-shop/media-01-placeholder.svg" | url }}" alt="Placeholder storefront grid — replace with final Schrift Shop screenshot" width="1440" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
